  "image_base": "0xffff800080000000",
  "review": "The base is KIMAGE_VADDR for 48-bit VAs (CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE unset); the tool also checks it against function-entry encodings. Reference offsets were found with --list and read against the v6.10 source: futex_hash loads futex_queues (ADD then LDR of __futex_data+0) and futex_init forms &__futex_data before storing futex_hashsize at +8. rcu_data: rcu_all_qs, rcu_qs and rcu_momentary_dyntick_idle form its per-CPU address (ADRP+ADD); rcu_all_qs then adds the BTF offset of rcu_urgent_qs (277) and TPIDR_EL1. kmalloc_size_index and kmalloc_caches: __kmalloc_noprof, __kmalloc_node_noprof and kmalloc_node_track_caller_noprof each form both addresses (ADRP+ADD, the inlined kmalloc_slab); the size index table ends where the cache table begins, and a live 144-byte kmalloc loads kmalloc_size_index[17] and kmalloc_caches[0][2] from them. hrtimer_bases has no reference of its own: its address is its BTF .data..percpu offset plus the section base that rcu_data's references fix. init_time_ns: __arm64_sys_futex forms its address (ADRP+ADD) for the inlined timens_ktime_to_host comparison.",
